{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Will you gouge out the eyes of those men?</b> Its meaning: Would you want to gouge out the eyes of those men — a hint to those who came out of Egypt, as if to say: Would you want to gouge out the eyes so that they not see, for this thing you have done to us is visible to the eyes. And by way of proverb they say: So-and-so's eyes are shut, therefore he does not see; therefore we will not go up. Some say: Would you want to darken the eyes so that they not see — meaning, you are performing a deception on us; we will not go up. Some say: Even if you had gouged out our eyes, we would not go up. And he said 'those men' in the manner of foolish people who are unwilling to speak about themselves in disparagement. And the correct one in my eyes: the word 'those men' is a hint to the elders who were with Moses, for so it is written: 'and the elders of Israel went after him.'" "<b>Nor to a land flowing with milk and honey.</b> The meaning: you have taken us out from a good place, and if you had brought us to a place as good as it and given us fields and vineyards as we had in Egypt, and you were seeking dominion — we would have borne it. But you removed us from a good place, from our fields and our vineyard, and you have not brought us to a place like it. Why do you seek dominion?"], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:01.142320775Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}